1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,755
In eighteen eighty seven, Svante Arrhenius gave the first modern definition.

2
00:00:05,755 --> 00:00:08,893
An acid gives hydrogen ions in water.

3
00:00:08,893 --> 00:00:11,770
A base gives hydroxide ions in water.

4
00:00:11,770 --> 00:00:15,690
It works for hydrochloric acid and sodium hydroxide.

5
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:20,156
But it fails in five ways, and the board asks about every one of them.

